    card title "How many have walked on the Moon?"

Hundreds of people have flown in space since 1961. But only a few have ever stood on the Moon.
    draw rocket y1961 moon

    erase rocket y1961

    ask "How many people have walked on the Moon? Set the counter." estimate.min 0 estimate.max 100 estimate.value 12 estimate.unit people store g default "30"
        right: Twelve. All of them American, and all between 1969 and 1972.
        wrong: It was twelve: all of them American, and all between 1969 and 1972.

    erase estimate_1 moon

Six Apollo crews landed, each putting two men on the surface while a third waited in orbit.
    draw twelve flag apollo m11 m12 m13 m14 m15 m16 m17 a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6 a7 a8 a9 a10 a11 a12

Every mission from Apollo 11 to 17 landed, but one.
    draw x13 x13b

Apollo 13 never got there. An oxygen tank exploded on the way, and the crew only just made it home.
    highlight m13

Neil Armstrong stepped out first, in July 1969, (@draw first@) and Buzz Aldrin followed him about twenty minutes later.

The last was Gene Cernan, in December 1972.
    text last "Cernan, 1972" #b5482e x 840 y 618 font_size 32

Before he climbed back in, he traced his daughter's initials in the lunar dust.
    text tdc "“TDC” in the dust" #b5482e x 790 y 200 font_size 34

No one has walked there since, in more than fifty years. So the club is still just twelve.
    highlight twelve

